      "mergeID": "610041a966a28559d4f0ce05",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Once a PCVR user use a Fallback avatar system, from then on they will continue to look like a Robot from Quest users, even if it is an Android-built avatar!\n\nFirst of all, Avatars that are not Android-built is rendered as fallback avatars for Quest users.\nAccording to the expected specification, if you change from fallback avatar A to Android-built avatar B, avatar B should be rendered without any problem.\nHowever, once fallback avatar A is loaded, no matter how many times the user changes to Android-built avatars B, C, D..., only the Robot will be displayed to Quest users.\nTo make matters worse, the Robot  can't be loaded even if you press \"Show Avatar\", and unless either one of the users leave the instance, once you wear the fallback avatar, you will continue to look like a Robot to Quest users.\nThis bug has been appearing since the mid-June 2021 update, and continues to plague Quest users as of Build1114.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "There is a serious problem with the fallback system on Quest",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "60d60cefd073b3552f133dc7",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
